ride": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "New Interests and Aspirations", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Restaurant Management Certificate", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Future Time Clauses,  As Soon As, Until", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use time clauses to give information about time and sequence in future actions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>, <span class=\"italic\">If</span>, <span class=\"italic\">When</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> Before and After </span>in time clauses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Future time clauses explain what needs to happen or which condition needs to be satisfied before a future event can occur.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the first conditional with these time clauses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br/> <ul>As soon as/Until/When/Before/After + Subject + Simple Present tense, Subject + will/be going to + Simple Present tense", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">As soon as</span> means almost at the same time. An action in the future will occur immediately after the action introduced by the time clause finishes. <br/> </br>Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul>As soon as I register, I will know for sure.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Until</span> means for the duration of an action. The action introduced by the time clause will lead to another action once it is completed. You normally use <span class=\"italic\">until </span>after the main clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">I'll keep coming to this class <span class=\"strong\">until </span>I hear from the registrar's office. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Before </span>means at an earlier time. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">After </span>means at a later time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> means on the condition that ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">When </span>means at the time of doing something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">After </span>I register at the college, I'll have a look at the syllabus for each course.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Oh and before I forget, when you visit this weekend, I will be working at the restaurant <span class=\"strong\">until </span>it closes. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> If </span>summer ever arrives, I'll be sailing a lot. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Future Continuous for Interrupted Action ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future. The action in the future is often interrupted by another action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment. When you use the Future Continuous, a future action can also be interrupted by another one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><span class=\"italic\">I'll be taking five courses when my mom comes to visit.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The ongoing action (taking five courses) is going to be interrupted the mom's visit.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are two ways to use the Future Continuous tense: <ul> <li>You use the Future Continuous to indicate that a longer action in the future will be interrupted by a shorter action in the future. </li></ul>Structure: will + be + present participle of the verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I will be working at the restaurant when you visit.</span><ul> <li>You use the Future Continuous to express the idea that two actions will be happening simultaneously. You use two Future Continuous actions in the same sentence.</li></ul> <br/> Structure:</br><ul> am/is/are + going to be + present participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">m going to be working </span>and studying when you'<span class=\"strong\">re going to be killing </span>time playing computer games.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I'm going to be working when you are there. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll be studying, attending class and working when you are killing time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I will be working at the restaurant. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I'll be taking five courses and working when my mom comes to visit.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "syllabus ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "(a \u200bplan \u200bshowing) the \u200bsubjects or \u200bbooks to be \u200bstudied in a \u200bparticular \u200bcourse, \u200bespecially a \u200bcourse that \u200bleads to an \u200bexam", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'll have a look at the syllabus for each course. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about education and school.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "textbook", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bbook used in a course of study that covered all topics in the course", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am going to have to buy all the textbooks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to register", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put \u200binformation, \u200bespecially \u200byour \u200bname, into an \u200bofficial \u200blist or \u200brecord", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  As soon as I register, I will know my schedule. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "elective", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a course that is optional for a program of study", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It looks like I will take three core courses and one or two electives.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lecture hall", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large room resembling a theater or concert hall with seats placed for listening to a speaker.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Business Communications course will be at the lecture hall in Boston on Tuesday evenings. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to kill time", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to do something that is not important, while waiting for time to pass", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll be studying, attending class and working when you are killing time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have one's nose in a book", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be reading or studying from books all the time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's too bad you won't have time because you'll have your nose in your books.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to crew", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to work as a team on a boat to keep it running properly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's too bad you won't have time to crew on the boat with me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to run around like a headless chicken", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to run about in a frenzied manner, distractedly, crazily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess we'll both be running around like headless chickens. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and research an English college or university for a course you would like to take.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes about the course including a description and the requirements to get into the course.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a friend about the course and explain why you want to take it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read about education.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes about a course. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about education.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}